    charter: `Territory reader for /lab: 102 files, 32,196 code lines + 6,580 comment lines, 43 routes, all shipped in the production build. Your charter is deliberately NOT "which rooms to delete" - the rooms are owner-approved design history indexed in src/app/lab/_registry.ts. Your questions are: (1) leakage - does any shipped (non-lab) file import from src/app/lab (grep -rn "app/lab" src --include=*.ts* excluding src/app/lab itself; also "@/app/lab"), and does any lab file import heavy things that end up in shared chunks; (2) cost - what do the lab routes add to build time and server bundle (raw/build.txt, raw/route-js.txt: lab pages first-load 700-1,340KB; .next/diagnostics/analyze/data/lab is 18MB of the 48MB analyzer output), and what would excluding them from production builds look like (a pageExtensions trick, an env-gated not-found in lab/layout.tsx, moving rooms out of app/ - lay out the options with trade-offs, including that /lab is used by the owner on the deployed site); (3) archived rooms - which registry entries are status "archived" and what their files still cost; (4) duplication of shipped primitives - rooms that were "picked" and transplanted verbatim (profiles/_variant-letterhead-3.tsx -> components/profile/letterhead-profile.tsx; landings variants -> components/landing; directory/_room -> components/directory; composer/_variants -> posts/create-post-form) now hold a second copy of production code that drifts; (5) LabRoomState (a Prisma model for lab state) and any lab-only lib; (6) the registry itself. Do not read all 32k lines line-by-line; read the registry, every page.tsx, and sample each room's biggest file enough to classify it. Record what you read.`,
